{
  "about": "Run report rows (CHECK-23, CHECK-24) and report publication (OUTPUT-10), moved from the run_report module of scalar_language.rs at a47519f5d, whose tests compared the saved report CSV line by line, the saved output CSV and the condition of the issues. A case whose test saved and read back every file it wrote states them as saved. One whose test read back only the output and some report rows builds and states the output table and the report rows of each kind its test compared, every column named: COUNT and TOTAL are int (CHECK-24), an empty cell is null, and an output cell takes its column's declared type. A failed run publishes only its report, keeping a primary file already there; a run that declares no report file writes none, though its report has the same rows as the declared run's, which its test compared equal; and a run that never read its input reports a missing count and null bytes. The schema-verification-log cases stage that benchmark with its spec.yaml edited, or its spec.yaml alone. Derived values: an undeclared run's out.csv is the CSV profile's header and one row, ID\\n1\\n; the grouped row_count's three check rows are the report's every check row, since the specification declares those three dataset verifications and no other check (CHECK-23); and a read that feeds another lookup or a predicate is two cases, one per column order of its test's loop. No engine output supplied these values.",
  "documents": {
    "one_column": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: input/input.csv}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n",
    "read_feeds": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nbase: SRC\nkeys: [ID]\ninput:\n  SRC: {path: input/src.csv, types: {ID: int}}\n  BASE: {path: input/base.csv, types: {ID: int, REF: int}}\n  RNG: {path: input/rng.csv, types: {ID: int, LO: int, HI: int}}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, V, F], report: report.csv}\nintermediates:\n  - id: Q\n    dataset: BASE\n    key: [ID]\n    filter: \"BASE.REF IS NOT NULL\"\n  - id: P\n    dataset: RNG\n    key: [ID]\n    between: {value: Q.REF, lower: LO, upper: HI}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: V, type: str, derivation: P.VAL}\n  - {name: F, type: str, derivation: {flag: {condition: \"P.VAL IS NOT NULL\", false_value: N, missing: N}}}\n"
  },
